/* ===================== IMPORTED TEMPLATE LIBRARY =====================
 *
 * 199 colony templates from four community repositories, stored as the EXACT
 * TEXT of the original files.
 *
 *   DalShooth     github.com/DalShooth/EVE_PI_Templates
 *   TheLegi0n-NBI github.com/TheLegi0n-NBI/PlayingWithPP
 *   josephdouce   github.com/josephdouce/eve-pi-templates
 *   Joakhan       github.com/Joakhan/eve_pi_templates
 *
 * WHY TEXT AND NOT PARSED OBJECTS
 *
 * The first version stored parsed JSON and re-serialised it on copy. That
 * silently broke every template: JavaScript has one Number type, so a file
 * containing "Diam": 8160.0 parses to 8160 and JSON.stringify writes "8160".
 * The ".0" is destroyed at parse time and cannot be recovered. Only
 * whole-number floats are affected, which is why it went unnoticed beside
 * values like 1.5655.
 *
 * The layout went too. These files come from EVE's own exporter, which is
 * neither pretty-printed nor compact: header on one line, then one object per
 * line inside "P" and "R". Re-serialising gave valid JSON in the wrong shape.
 *
 * Keeping the text removes the guesswork. A byte-for-byte copy of a file
 * known to work needs no assumptions about what EVE's parser tolerates.
 *
 * Only edits: line endings normalised to \n, surrounding whitespace trimmed.
 *
 * COMMAND CENTER V ONLY
 * 40 templates written for Command Center IV were dropped. Supporting two
 * skill levels means every product appears twice with no way for a reader to
 * tell which one their character can actually run.
 *
 * 293 files in, 199 out: 53 byte-identical copies, 40 CC4, and one layout
 * present in two repos merged under both credits.
 */
